# Deployment

- Run the backend and the frontend as Docker containers on one machine.
- The database is the SQLite file described in the database rule. It has no container and no published port.
- That machine may be a Raspberry Pi or a much stronger server. Write for the small machine: little CPU, little memory, little disk, and no idle work.
- Serve the application on the local network.
- Add a process or a container only when the backend or the frontend needs it.
- The frontend, backend, and database are decided in their own rules. Ports and resource numbers are not decided yet. Wait for a later rule before choosing them.
